 "measures": [
  {
   "name": "Public Measure WD",
   "jurisdiction": "Sergeant Bluff-Luton Community School District",
   "ballotLanguage": "Shall the Board of Directors of the Sergeant Bluff-Luton Community School District in the County of Woodbury, State of Iowa, be authorized to contract indebtedness and issue General Obligation Bonds in an amount not to exceed $38,000,000 to provide funds to build, furnish, and equip a new Primary School building as an addition to the Elementary building (including demolition of the existing Primary building) and improve the site?"
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Source: 73 per-precinct official sample ballot PDFs (text-extractable). Board of Supervisors District 2 and District 4 contests both appear on every precinct ballot in the county, i.e. supervisors are elected countywide (at-large) with district residency requirements; all voters see both. Township offices appear only on ballots of precincts in that township; empty candidate lists are write-in only (Banner, Moville trustee, Grange clerk/vacancy, Rock clerk, Morgan clerk, Liston clerk, Little Sioux, Oto). Public Measure WD (SBL school bond) appears on 8 precinct ballots (29B, 29C, 30, 31, 32C, 32D, 33B, 37C). No county-level measure."
}